# The checks that ship-pr's `pr-review.sh checks` and `merge` treat as advisory on this
# repository's PRs, one ERE per line; a name any line matches is advisory. The lines replace the
# script's default list, so the first spells the default names in. The second matches every job of
# .github/workflows/macos-weekly.yml (named `bash 3.2 suites, <part> (macos)`): the maintainer's
# decision is that a PR merges without waiting for the macOS runner queue. Since ludics#974 those
# jobs run weekly and on dispatch, never on a push or a pull request, so a push run of
# skill-scripts.yml carries none of them (and the fleet-worker gate's `base --advisory-red`, which
# also reads this file, ludics-lite#651 and #659, finds none there); the line keeps the check runs
# a dispatch puts on a PR head from holding its merge.
# Read from the default branch: a PR's edit to this file applies only once that PR has merged.
# Re-check it when the workflows' job names change. No required job may `needs:` a macOS job
# (the boundary in SHIP_PR_ADVISORY_CHECKS's entry in pr-review.sh's usage text).
^(claude|Claude Code|github pages docs)$
^bash 3\.2 suites, .* \(macos\)$
